  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0361' contains four tables: 'Restaurant', 'User_review', 'Dish', and 'Review_reply'.\nThe 'Restaurant' table represents a collection of restaurants. It contains columns for the restaurant's address, average cost, business hours, name, phone number, and a unique identifier (Restaurant_ID).\nThe 'User_review' table holds reviews made by users. It includes columns for the review's actual photos (in BLOB format), dining time (in DATETIME format), rating (in FLOAT format), a unique identifier (Review_ID), and the content of the review (in VARCHAR format).\nThe 'Dish' table represents dishes served by the restaurants. It includes columns for the category of the dish, description, a unique identifier (Dish_ID), the URL of the dish image, monthly sales (in FLOAT format), name, price (in FLOAT format), the identifier of the restaurant serving the dish (Restaurant_ID), and the satisfaction rate (in FLOAT format). The Restaurant_ID column is a foreign key referencing the Restaurant table.\nFinally, the 'Review_reply' table holds replies to user reviews. It includes columns for a unique identifier (Reply_ID), the content of the reply (in VARCHAR format), the time of the reply (in DATETIME format), and the identifier of the review being replied to (Review_ID_being_replied_to). The Review_ID_being_replied_to column is a foreign key referencing the User_review table.\nAll columns allow null values except for the Restaurant_ID and Review_ID_being_replied_to in the 'Dish' and 'Review_reply' tables respectively. The primary keys are the unique identifiers in their respective tables. Referential integrity is maintained through foreign key references.",
  "gold_question": "This is a restaurant recommendation system for managing restaurant information and recommending nearby restaurants. For basic restaurant information management, the system maintains restaurant basic information, including restaurant ID, name, address, phone number, business hours, and average cost per person. It records restaurant geographical location information including latitude and longitude coordinates, manages restaurant feature tags such as \"Sichuan cuisine\", \"hot pot\", \"family gathering\", etc., and tracks restaurant ratings and number of reviews. For dish management, the system records information about dishes offered by each restaurant, including dish ID, name, price, description, etc. It adds category tags to dishes such as \"signature dish\", \"best-seller\", \"new arrival\", etc., supports uploading dish images, and records dish satisfaction rate and monthly sales. For user review management, the system supports users to rate and review restaurants, recording review content, rating, dining time, and other information. It supports uploading actual dining photos, and allows restaurants to reply to reviews, including reply time and content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0361.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0361\nCREATE TABLE `Restaurant` (\n  `Restaurant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `average_cost` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `business_hours` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Restaurant_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_review` (\n  `Review_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `dining_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `photos` blob DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Review_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Dish` (\n  `Dish_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `monthly_sales` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `satisfaction_rate` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Restaurant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Dish_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Dish_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Restaurant_ID`) REFERENCES `Restaurant` (`Restaurant_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Review_reply` (\n  `Reply_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reply_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Review_ID_being_replied_to` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Reply_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Review_reply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Review_ID_being_replied_to`) REFERENCES `User_review` (`Review_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
